From f60f4ea568cd57be365b21aa80532bab148fb781 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:59:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] spec_lanes: STRATA_SPEC_LANES=2 alone stays M1b, shared
 VRAM by default for 3-4; review fixes (opt-in STRATA_SPEC_LANES=2..4)

STRATA_LC_SHARE defaults on only for 3 and 4 lanes; with it off every lane has
its own arena, KEEP=0, M1b's boot rule, no boot capture of the solo pipeline's
graphs and lane graphs up to --spec, so production's STRATA_SPEC_LANES=2 +
STRATA_SOLO_PIPELINE=1 is M1b. Lanes 2 and 3's drafters load after the expert
caches and count in the lane fit. GDN snapshots in lane 2's arena stay below
its persistent tail. The post-build check treats an unreadable card as short.
A failed snapshot move-back frees what it moved. HOLD=2 is M1b's rule again.
STRATA_SPEC_LANES folds the solo pipeline in only where the lanes can run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
